"""Present original-scene and CLEAR-scene execution with measured outcomes."""
from pathlib import Path
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];soup=BeautifulSoup((root/'index.html').read_text(),'html.parser');article=soup.find(id='method-execution')
process=article.find(id='mpc-process');process_html=str(process) if process else ''
parts=['<h3>(d) Execution and replanning</h3><p class="method-lead">The controller tracks object targets and updates its commands from new observations.</p>']
# Matches the archived CLEAR controller's _evaluate_controls and _cost, with smoothing disabled.
parts.append(r'''<div class="mpc-objective"><div class="mpc-objective-row"><div class="equation" data-tex="J(\delta\mathbf u)=\underbrace{\lambda_p\mathcal L_{\rm path}}_{\text{Path progress}}+\frac1H\sum_{k=1}^{H}\left[\underbrace{\lambda_c\mathcal L_{\rm contact}^k}_{\text{Palm contact}}+\underbrace{\lambda_t\mathcal L_{\rm tilt}^k+\lambda_s\mathcal L_{\rm unsafe}^k}_{\text{Stability}}+\underbrace{\lambda_w\mathcal L_{\rm wall}^k+\lambda_o\mathcal L_{\rm other}^k}_{\text{Scene clearance}}+\underbrace{\lambda_u\lVert\delta u_k\rVert_2^2}_{\text{Control effort}}\right]"></div><aside class="mpc-objective-notation" aria-label="Objective notation"><span data-tex="\delta\mathbf u^\star=\arg\min_{\delta\mathbf u}J(\delta\mathbf u)"></span><dl><dt>δu</dt><dd>Residual commands</dd><dt>H</dt><dd>Forecast steps</dd><dt>λ</dt><dd>Term weights</dd><dt>k</dt><dd>Forecast index</dd></dl></aside></div><p class="method-small-copy">CLEAR evaluates predicted object progress, contact alignment, stability, clearance, and command effort. It applies the first control segment and replans from the next observation.</p><details class="method-details"><summary>Objective terms in these replays</summary><p>This is the objective used by the recorded CLEAR controller. SUMO uses its upstream task reward. LA-QDPP controls candidate retention and is not an additional term in J. These recordings use a 0.6 s prediction horizon with six 0.1 s control steps. Optional temporal smoothing is disabled.</p><div class="equation" data-tex="\mathcal L_{\rm contact}^{k}=\min_{\pi\in S_2}\sum_{h\in\{L,R\}}\lVert p_h^k-c_{\pi(h)}^k\rVert_2,\qquad\mathcal L_{\rm tilt}^{k}=\lVert(g_x^k,g_y^k)\rVert_2"></div><p>The two p values are the tracked hand link positions and c values are the object attached contact targets. The pairing with lower total distance is used. The gravity vector g is expressed in the robot frame.</p><div class="equation" data-tex="\mathcal L_{\rm unsafe}^{k}=\mathbf1[g_z^k&gt;-0.8]+\mathbf1[(R_o^k)_{zz}&lt;0.8],\quad\mathcal L_{\rm wall}^{k}=\sum_b\max\{0,0.06-\min_w d_{bw}^k\},\quad\mathcal L_{\rm other}^{k}=\sum_{o\ne o^\star}\lVert x_o^k-x_o^0\rVert_2"></div><p>Unsafe states penalize robot tilt and object tipping. Signed wall distances are evaluated at robot links. Other objects are penalized for moving from their initial horizontal positions.</p><div class="equation" data-tex="\mathcal L_{\rm path}=\frac1H\sum_{k=1}^{H}\left[d(q_o^k,r_{i_k})+\sum_{j=i_k}^{M-1}d(r_j,r_{j+1})\right],\quad d(a,b)=\sqrt{\lVert a_{xy}-b_{xy}\rVert_2^2+2\operatorname{wrap}(a_\theta-b_\theta)^2}"></div><p>The waypoint index i advances as predicted object poses reach the reference and is clamped to the final reference after completion. The remaining reference length discourages stopping just before a waypoint. Residual commands are the normalized controls used by these recordings.</p></details></div>''')

groups=[('SUMO original box scene','A 1 m box with mass 10 kg starts 1 m from the goal. The baseline uses the upstream box scene and reset. Our controller is transferred to the same box geometry, mass, inertia, friction, and relative layout in its own runtime.',[
 ('mpc-stock-optimized','MPC w/ optimization (ours)','0.70 m moved · 0.34 m goal error · 60.1 s','The controller maintains bilateral palm contact but reaches its time limit.'),
 ('mpc-stock-baseline','MPC (SUMO)','0.70 m moved · 0.30 m goal error · 9.36 s','The original task reports success at its 0.30 m position tolerance and low object velocity.')]),
 ('CLEAR two gate scene','The same two gate development scene used by the controller comparison. The replay follows the first object interaction, with a 2 m reference path.',[
 ('mpc-optimized','MPC w/ optimization (ours)','1.97 m moved · 0.07 m goal error · 14.0 s','Contact conditioned targets guide the arms along the object reference.'),
 ('mpc-baseline','MPC (SUMO)','0.70 m moved · 1.33 m goal error · 40.0 s','Contact is lost at 14.14 s. The box is stationary from 15 s onward while the recording continues to 40 s. This is a failed attempt with subsequent robot motion, not 40 s of pushing.')])]
parts.append('<div class="mpc-scenes-grid">')
for title,intro,rows in groups:
 parts.append(f'<section class="mpc-scene-comparison"><h4>{title}</h4><p class="method-small-copy">{intro}</p><div class="experiment-matrix paired-matrix mpc-comparison">')
 for scene,label,metrics,detail in rows:
  inset='Robot chase view' if scene.endswith('baseline') else 'Ego RGB + paired palm regions'
  parts.append(f'''<article><h5>{label}</h5><div class="viewer experiment-viewer" data-scene="{scene}" data-title="{label}" data-ego="true"><video class="preview-video" muted playsinline controls data-autoplay preload="none" poster="assets/media/{scene}.png"><source src="assets/media/{scene}.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video><button class="launch" type="button">Play in 3D</button><figure class="ego-inset"><video muted playsinline preload="none" poster="assets/media/{scene}-ego.png"><source src="assets/media/{scene}-ego.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video><figcaption>{inset}</figcaption></figure></div><p class="mpc-outcome">{metrics}</p><p class="method-small-copy">{detail}</p></article>''')
 if rows[-1][0]=='mpc-baseline':
  parts[-1]=parts[-1].replace('</article>','<div class="mpc-contact-bookmarks" aria-label="Recorded contact events"><button type="button" data-mpc-seek="5">Pushing · 5 s</button><button type="button" data-mpc-seek="14.14">Contact lost · 14.14 s</button></div></article>')
 parts.append('</div></section>')
parts.append('</div>')
parts.append('''<p class="figure-caption">Videos preserve recorded durations. Smooth video frames interpolate measured poses. Play in 3D exposes the candidate trajectories, five reference anchors, and a synchronized contact view. Each result describes one seed and one scene, rather than aggregate benchmark performance.</p><details class="method-details"><summary>Controller settings and comparison scope</summary><p>The upstream G1 box task disables explicit left and right arm commands. Its MPC controls three base velocities, while the native G1 policy controls the limbs. Both replays preserve measured body contacts. In the CLEAR scene, the last target contact occurs at 14.14 s. From 15 s to the endpoint, the robot travels another 1.08 m while the box remains at rest. This setting permits pushing with the body and explains why it does not independently reach with both arms. The original task succeeds within 0.30 m in each horizontal coordinate when object speed is below 0.10 m/s. Our controller uses a stricter 0.08 m goal tolerance and a 0.12 rad orientation tolerance.</p><p>Our controller uses contact conditioned Cartesian targets and LA-QDPP selection, with a 0.6 s horizon and a 0.1 s control interval. SUMO uses its native G1 policy, box reward, and Judo CEM, with a 2.5 s horizon and a 0.05 s control interval. Both evaluate 24 candidates. The original scene comparison retains each runtime’s robot initialization and contact solver. The CLEAR scene is expressed in a rigid goal centered frame for SUMO. These comparisons include differences in runtime, reward, action representation, stopping conditions, and timing. They do not isolate the selector.</p><p>The optimized 3D replay includes recomputed contact scores and outlined palm neighborhoods. The SUMO detail view follows the robot from behind. All robot and object motion comes from physical execution records. The CLEAR scene is a development example and is not reported as held out benchmark performance.</p></details>''')
parts.append(process_html)
article.clear();article.append(BeautifulSoup(''.join(parts),'html.parser'));article['data-compact']='true'
from refine_method_presentation import refine
refine(soup)
(root/'index.html').write_text(str(soup).rstrip()+'\n')
